        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 45,
        "headingId": 542,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T17:40:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 504,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 543,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69252,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 45,
        "headingId": 543,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T17:40:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 505,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 544,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69253,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 45,
        "headingId": 544,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Paediatric cystic nephroma is localized to the kidney.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T17:40:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 506,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 545,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69254,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 45,
        "headingId": 545,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The typical presentation is that of an abdominal mass. The purely cystic nature of the lesion may be evident on imaging studies.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T17:40:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 507,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 546,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69255,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 45,
        "headingId": 546,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Paediatric cystic nephroma occurs slightly more commonly in boys than in girls. Most patients are aged &lt;&nbsp;24&nbsp;months.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T17:40:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 508,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 547,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69256,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 45,
        "headingId": 547,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Approximately 90% of paediatric cystic nephromas harbour <em>DICER1</em> mutations; most (two&nbsp;thirds) of these are associated with a germline mutation. Familial cystic nephroma {8382107} associated with germline <em>DICER1</em> mutations {21266384; 21036787} may be bilateral. <em>DICER1</em> syndrome includes susceptibility to pleuropulmonary blastoma, Sertoli&ndash;Leydig cell tumour, and other neoplasms.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T17:40:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 509,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 548,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69257,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 45,
        "headingId": 548,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>DICER1</em> mutations specific to paediatric cystic nephroma have not been found in cystic partially differentiated nephroblastoma {24481001} or lesions known as adult cystic nephroma {28177962}, supporting its distinctive nature. Mouse models with conditional ablation of <em>DICER1</em> in ureteric bud epithelium during development show cystic masses of the kidney that resemble cystic nephroma {20944551}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T17:40:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 516,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 555,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69258,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 45,
        "headingId": 555,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Paediatric cystic nephromas have a median diameter of approximately 90&nbsp;mm {6294736; 1846992; 19172100} and a median weight of approximately 500&nbsp;g {26772403}. They are usually well circumscribed and consist entirely of cysts of variable size; the septa are thin and there are no expansile, solid nodules to alter the rounded contour of the cysts {9503503}. Lesions frequently herniate into the renal pelvis.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T17:40:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 510,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 549,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69259,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 45,
        "headingId": 549,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most paediatric cystic nephromas are well demarcated microscopically by a fibrous pseudocapsule {26772403}, but a minority lack a pseudocapsule, either partially or completely. They are composed entirely of septated cysts lined by flattened, cuboidal, or hobnail epithelium, or they are denuded. The septa contain fibrous tissue with focal cellular condensations and well-differentiated tubules. The stroma labels for ER like many other cystic renal lesions. The presence of immature nephroblastic elements excludes the diagnosis of paediatric cystic nephroma and indicates cystic partially differentiated nephroblastoma {2544253}. The lesions known as adult cystic nephromas belong to the mixed epithelial and stromal tumour family; unlike paediatric cystic nephroma, they typically contain ropy collagen and label for inhibin {28177962}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T17:40:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 511,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 550,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69260,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 45,
        "headingId": 550,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T17:40:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 512,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 551,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69261,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 45,
        "headingId": 551,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Demonstration of <em>DICER1</em> mutation is helpful in some cases.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T17:40:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 515,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 554,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69262,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 45,
        "headingId": 554,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> paediatric cystic nephromas must lack solid nodules on gross or microscopic examination; septa may contain mature tubules but no primitive blastemal elements.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> the presence of <em>DICER1</em> mutations is supportive but not required.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T17:40:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 513,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 552,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69263,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 45,
        "headingId": 552,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T17:40:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 514,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 553,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69264,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 45,
        "headingId": 553,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Paediatric cystic nephroma is treated with surgery only, usually by complete nephrectomy or (in selected cases) by partial nephrectomy {19172100}. Its prognosis is excellent, with 100% event-free and overall survival {17162067}. Very rare cases of cystic nephroma transformation into <em>DICER1</em> sarcoma have been described, but the risk is regarded as very low {24481001}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T17:40:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]